text:
Maya (Support): FYI — AcmeFinance reported a tool invocation failure when creating invoices. They get a validation error from our gateway. Here are the top lines from their error: `ValidationError: /params/billing_profile: expected object, got array`

Liam (Eng): Can you paste the payload they sent and the exact error blob? Might be a client-side shape problem.

Maya (Support): Pasting sanitized payload and the gateway response below. Note: customer is on SDK v0.9.7.
```json
{
  "action": "create_invoice",
  "params": {
    "customer_id": "acme-123",
    "billing_profile": [
      { "id": "bp-999", "method": "card" }
    ],
    "line_items": [
      { "description": "monthly subscription", "amount_cents": 5000 }
    ]
  }
}
```
Gateway response: 
```
HTTP 400 Bad Request
{
  "error": {
    "message": "tool call failed schema validation",
    "details": [
      { "path": "/params/billing_profile", "expected": "object", "received": "array" }
    ]
  }
}
```

Ravi (Platform): That schema (func schema for create_invoice) expects billing_profile to be a single object (object with id/method). Looks like the SDK serializes singletons as arrays in some codepath (we saw a similar bug with promo codes).

Nora (SRE): Any latency/error spikes correlated? ci-bot shows no repeat rate increase — this looks per-customer.

Maya (Support): Customer timeline: sent request at 2026-03-11T15:22:03Z, retried twice, still fails. Wants a repro and a short-term workaround.

Liam (Eng): Repro notes for Eng: I tried the same shape to our local function runner and get the same validation error. The function signature uses JSON Schema: 
```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "billing_profile": { "type": "object" },
    "line_items": { "type": "array" }
  },
  "required": ["billing_profile", "line_items"]
}
```
When billing_profile is an array it fails as expected.

Liam (Eng): Quick mitigation options: 1) advise customer to change SDK call to pass object not array (fast). 2) Add a small server-side compatibility shim that accepts a single-element array and coerces to object for this specific field (short-lived). 3) Patch SDK to stop wrapping singletons in arrays (medium).

Maya (Support): Customer cannot update SDK immediately (locked environment). They prefer server-side shim or a proxy change. Can we do a targeted compatibility fallback for this function only?

Ravi (Platform): We can add a targeted coercion rule in the function invocation layer — a safe transform: if billing_profile is array of length 1 and schema expects object, replace it with the array[0]. I'll open a canary for staging. Needs review: ensure no legitimate array-of-objects case is silently transformed.

Liam (Eng): Please scope to func name create_invoice and field path /params/billing_profile only. Add logging and a feature flag so we can turn off quickly. Also include a metric for coerced_count.

Maya (Support): Thanks. I told the customer we can enable a server-side shim behind a flag for their account, and that engineering will monitor coercions. They asked for ETA.

Ravi (Platform): ETA: canary to staging in ~2 hours, if green we can enable for the customer in the next maintenance window (low risk). I'll attach PR and references in the ticket.

ci-bot: Deployment scheduled: validation-coerce-billingprofile (canary) -> staging at 2026-03-11T17:35:00Z :rocket: 

Nora (SRE): After canary, watch error rate and coerced_count metric. If coerced_count > 0 for other customers we may need to rollback.

Maya (Support): I'll email the customer the short-term plan and post the internal ticket. If they accept the shim we'll enable per-account and follow up on SDK patch timeline.

Liam (Eng): Follow-up: create a checklist in the ticket: repro steps, schema excerpt, SDK versions impacted, canary PR link, metric names, rollback plan.

Maya (Support): Added checklist to ticket #INC-2026-119. Closing loop here — will update when canary completes. :thumbsup:
